modules and package    
what are modules and packages
module:-
every python file is itself a module.
we can export the class name, function name ,object name ,variable constants in the global scope
and can be then imported in any other considering this file as a module.


every module can have two types of functionality


1. can  be exported a module

2. can be executed as a program


now if we want to execute the module as well then we can use the concept main execution


every file which is executed called the __main__instance.

packages:-


collection of multiple modules put in a  folder is said to be packageds.


xyz

a.py ->m1
b.py ->m2
c.py ->m3


sub package : folder inside folder   
pqr

xyz
a.py
b.py
c.py


rules of package:  foldername shoudld not contain any special character no spaces , it should be lower case but module can be upper lower case or combination .
after python version 3.5.x it is mandatory that  a package should contain a special file called __init__.py



pdbc (python database connectivity)


1.pdbc starts for the python database connectivity.
2.this concept remains same in every programmiing language like java: jdbc

3.in pdbc other python application will connect to real time database like ( mysql,sqlserver,oracle or postgressql,Ssqlite)
4.it is a database driver which is convert python calls to databse calls and databse calls to python native calls.

python app<---------------->Databse
           <-----request-----> 
	   <-----response---->

# python sent request to databse for like read ,insert ,delete the databse reponse it .

 which type of database : it is always RDBS relational database management system  (sql)
 databse: mysql
 for nosql for eg mongodb ,dynamodb,redis,rabbitmqt ,memcache,couchdb,cassendra,bhive,hbase,we have different driver.
 
 database is a technology that at server level.
 in order to make any system server we need server wala software.
 
 1. mysql database
 2.server (IIS,ngnix,apache) in all world this are three types of servers .
 3. sql client (sql workbench,phpmyadmin,mysql terminal,heidisql)
 
 
 we are aware that software technology is platform dependent.
 
 os: windows   mysql.exe
 linux: ubantu  mysql.deb or mysql.rpm
 macos: apple mysql.app
 
 any configuration in app made for one type of platform will be changed when we deploy the application
 to the server because there can be the chance that ,server and local system may have different configuration .
  
  
__init__.py : can be blank but this file must exist
 importance: the code written in this file  is automatically called as package imported.



